WEBVTT

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:09.750
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:20.280
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.470
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:06.950
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:14.220
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:20.950
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:28.390
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:44.330
Yun!

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:51.000
<b>Pair</b>

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:54.510
But that’s Yun.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:55.730
Yun!

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:56.930
No way…

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:58.050
Where’s Onasia?

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.510
What’s become of Onasia, Yun?

00:02:00.510 --> 00:02:03.010
And why are you…

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.520
I think I know why.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.020
You decided this is where
you want to be, right, Yun?

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.690
Roatreamon, what do you mean?

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.660
Yun has made her choice.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:17.460
She’s chosen her own path.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.540
I am here now.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:31.040
That’s right. Yun’s right there.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.040
Let’s go.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:40.430
Maybe…

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:44.360
…I should’ve come here before
with all my friends from Rubor.

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.700
Let’s go in together.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.310
Yes!

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.650
Paraietta, you’ve been
through a lot, haven’t you?

00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:02.570
I think we all have.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.660
Morinas, you don’t have
any regrets, do you?

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:12.370
Well, I did want to pray to
the skies in an ancient Simoun.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.670
I mean I wanted to operate one!

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:21.290
I always wanted to sit in the captain’s
chair on the Arcus Prima, just once!

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:25.640
Come on!

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:28.140
Knock it off, both of you!

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.640
But…

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:31.140
I…

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.350
I feel…

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:36.650
…as if I don’t know
anything about any of you.

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:39.650
Right.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:44.190
We don’t really know
anything about each other.

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:50.120
But we must all fall if
we ever want to understand.

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.170
We must fall.

00:03:54.070 --> 00:03:55.880
Uttering screams along the way…

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:58.170
Even as we’re racked by fear…

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.170
With our hearts in our mouths…

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:04.180
We must hold on to ourselves and
keep falling and falling endlessly.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:06.680
And as you continue to fall…

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:09.730
You reach out and cling to something…

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:13.690
…because you’re so afraid,
and you try to hang on somehow.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:17.750
But we have to let go
eventually, don’t we?

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:22.700
Somewhere at the bottom of that
abyss, I promise you I’ll be waiting.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:25.700
Big Sister…

00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:08.220
The priestesses of Chor Tempest…

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:11.930
Actually, I suppose we shouldn’t
be calling them that anymore.

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:14.890
But yes, they should be returning soon.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:17.590
I’m looking forward to finding out…

00:06:17.590 --> 00:06:20.480
…what decision each of the
priestesses of Chor Tempest has made.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.020
Yes, I’m looking forward to that too.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:25.980
And what about those two?

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:30.490
I think they’re going to be
our last responsibility here.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.570
Yes.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.300
At the Spring…

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:54.730
Yun was supporting us, wasn’t she?

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:55.640
Yes.

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:57.650
It almost felt like being in a cradle.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:01.560
All of our emotions,
all at the same time!

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:12.820
Listen, we’re…

00:08:03.150 --> 00:08:05.830
I am here now.

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.350
What’s the matter, Aer?

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:26.860
Aer?

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:34.730
Tell me!

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:35.910
What?

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:39.080
Tell me why my heart hurts so much!

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.370
You know the answer, don’t you?

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.830
Yes.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:43.910
Why?

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:46.880
Why is it that my heart
is hurting so much?

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:50.990
Because you’re in love.

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.630
This is love?

00:08:56.340 --> 00:09:00.350
Yes. That’s what love is, Aer.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:04.770
I love you!

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:07.740
And I love you.

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:32.840
Amuria… She was a
strong person, wasn’t she?

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:35.050
Yes, she was.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:37.430
She was a strong person.

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:52.270
Secretly meeting with
a highland priestess…

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:55.400
…and before Tempus Spatium too?

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:57.700
That can’t be the
action of a sane person.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.490
I believe…

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:06.080
…this will be my last task for
the Chor Tempest Simoun sibyllae.

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:11.080
I hope that Tempus
Spatium will be forgiving.

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:17.630
I can’t forget what Sibylla
Neviril said during the hearing.

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:25.470
I am not looking to blame
anyone for this war we’re waging.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:27.640
No matter how tragic and
painful our lives may be now…

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.770
…I believe that it was
all meant to happen this way.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:32.880
Whether or not that is the
will of Tempus Spatium…

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:36.060
…it makes no difference to me now.

00:10:36.840 --> 00:10:40.990
I no longer even care whether
it’s God’s will anymore…

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:44.330
However, I do have one
question for you all.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:46.990
Despite all this…

00:10:46.990 --> 00:10:49.750
…can I still call
myself a Simoun sibylla?

00:10:58.630 --> 00:10:59.750
Guragief…

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:08.770
I have a feeling you never
stopped being a sibylla, even now.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:15.980
Yes?

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:20.490
Oh, Paraietta!

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:22.030
I’m back.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:24.780
We’re all waiting on
the observation deck.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:25.880
Okay.

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.040
Paraietta!

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:33.540
I’m back, Neviril.

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:37.210
I think I’ll go on ahead!

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.550
You guys can join us later.

00:11:39.550 --> 00:11:42.550
Would you do that, Aer?

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:44.260
See you!

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:46.810
I’ll see you later too, Paraietta.

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.220
Right.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:52.730
Will you dance with me?

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:55.020
Yes.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:18.670
The soldiers are watching.

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:20.090
I don’t mind.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:22.590
Does it bother you, Neviril?

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:25.590
No, not really.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:31.100
There are still two priestesses
who have not yet entered the Spring.

00:12:31.100 --> 00:12:35.350
Yes, Sibylla Neviril and Sibylla Aer.

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:41.860
When do they plan to
make their pilgrimage?

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:44.700
Welcome back, everyone!

00:12:49.990 --> 00:12:51.410
How was the city?

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:54.660
Everyone seemed really happy.

00:12:54.660 --> 00:12:57.170
Yes, so many smiling faces!

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:59.670
Were you bored, Aer?

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:04.760
Well, I did some maju by
myself and then had some tea.

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:08.260
You guys haven’t really
changed much. Uh…

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:10.810
I chose to become a woman.

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:12.270
I chose to become a woman too.

00:13:12.270 --> 00:13:14.020
And I…

00:13:15.270 --> 00:13:16.310
Male?

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:17.400
Right!

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:20.150
I chose to become male also.

00:13:20.150 --> 00:13:21.400
I see…

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:30.420
They’ll go as soon as
they feel ready to do so.

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:31.870
We cannot wait.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:36.370
This is the most crucial
condition in our peace treaty.

00:13:36.370 --> 00:13:43.300
Yes, but it’s not as if a time limit has
been set for that condition to be met.

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:49.140
We cannot wait.

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.810
The reason I didn’t choose Aer…

00:13:55.810 --> 00:14:00.310
…wasn’t because I didn’t
want to betray you once again.

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:04.820
It was simply an excuse to
protect myself from getting hurt.

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.640
I just wanted to be a good girl.

00:14:09.280 --> 00:14:10.320
Can you imagine?

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:26.730
Wanting to be a good
girl all the time…

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:28.720
How childish is that?

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:33.220
I was sure that both Amuria and
Aer had chosen me as their pair…

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.100
…just as a tool…

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:39.440
…to complete the Emerald Ri Majon.

00:14:40.350 --> 00:14:41.640
But I was wrong.

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:45.840
I was the one who was drawn
to their single-mindedness!

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:50.790
I came to realize that they’re
both far more pure in spirit than I.

00:14:52.790 --> 00:14:56.950
Neither of them are
afraid of getting hurt.

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:00.020
Yes, exactly, Paraietta.

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:05.130
I’ve made up my mind to be true
to what I’m feeling right now.

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:09.470
Once you stop trying to subject
others to your own feelings…

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:13.180
…you start to feel as if you can
plant your feet on a bigger stage.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:15.970
I’m not going to wait and be
consumed by the waiting anymore.

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:21.980
And I’m going to stop blaming
everything on the one I love.

00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:25.980
Because I want to learn what
it’s like to be truly loved.

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:31.450
Paraietta! Did you…

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:32.490
Yes.

00:15:35.200 --> 00:15:37.330
I chose to stay female.

00:15:37.990 --> 00:15:41.840
We will arrange for them to be
escorted to the Spring by nightfall.

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.750
Our soldiers will accompany them.

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:01.940
I chose to become a woman.

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:03.790
Right.

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.610
Me too. I chose to become a woman too.

00:16:08.230 --> 00:16:09.570
I see!

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.120
Welcome home.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:25.130
I’m back.

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:31.210
What do you want?

00:16:31.210 --> 00:16:32.630
Neviril!

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:34.630
Let go of me!

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:36.140
Aer!

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:37.930
Neviril!

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:39.140
Neviril!

00:16:42.570 --> 00:16:46.190
Sibylla Aurea, please wait here for now.

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:54.280
Let go of me, you morons!

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:56.320
Aer…

00:16:56.320 --> 00:16:57.510
Let go!

00:17:00.550 --> 00:17:01.790
Aer…

00:17:15.130 --> 00:17:16.160
Aer…

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:04.930
No! They can’t make Neviril
and Aer go to the Spring.

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:06.140
Right!

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:07.890
Those two are our…

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:11.190
That’s right. They’re carrying
our present on their shoulders!

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:15.740
Paraietta, is this really part of the
peace treaty that Simulacrum agreed to?

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:17.900
Yeah, can they really do this?

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:20.740
Neviril and Aer…

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:23.910
…will only go to that
Spring over my dead body!

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:28.750
The eternal present…

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:31.750
Aer…

00:18:33.280 --> 00:18:35.760
I love you.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:38.760
Aer…

00:18:42.790 --> 00:18:45.020
I want to see you, Neviril!

00:18:46.190 --> 00:18:49.310
I want to touch you, Neviril!

00:18:50.770 --> 00:18:51.800
Aer…

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:56.770
Neviril…

00:19:25.900 --> 00:19:27.430
Don’t do it, Alty!

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.420
Now what should we do?

00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:54.920
Captain!

00:19:55.700 --> 00:19:59.960
That title is no longer
appropriate for me.

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:01.800
But…

00:20:02.570 --> 00:20:05.450
We have asked permission
to give our sibyllae…

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:08.430
…a final farewell before
they go to the Spring.

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:13.810
That’s the most the Arcus Prima’s
captain could manage to do for them.

00:20:54.230 --> 00:20:57.150
How uncharacteristically
barbaric of you!

00:20:57.690 --> 00:20:58.730
I suppose.

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:01.570
Aer…

00:21:02.280 --> 00:21:03.320
Right!

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:05.820
Let’s go.

00:21:11.790 --> 00:21:12.830
Thank you!

00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:14.830
Please hurry!

00:21:23.420 --> 00:21:25.340
Aer! Neviril!

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:27.590
Paraietta!

00:21:28.290 --> 00:21:30.310
Floe, Alty.

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:33.140
Don’t cry, Floe.

00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:34.230
But…

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:35.310
I said don’t cry!

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:36.890
Morinas.

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:39.150
We’re counting on you!

00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:41.110
Roatreamon…

00:21:41.830 --> 00:21:43.940
I suppose this is
goodbye, Sibylla Aurea.

00:21:44.540 --> 00:21:46.610
Farewell, both of you.

00:21:47.310 --> 00:21:49.160
I know you two can do it!

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:51.950
Vura, Kaim.

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:53.870
Paraietta.

00:21:55.280 --> 00:21:57.620
Farewell, Aer…

00:21:58.480 --> 00:21:59.880
Neviril…

00:22:00.850 --> 00:22:01.880
Farewell.

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:05.920
I promise you, someday,
we’ll meet again…

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:13.510
Take care of yourselves.

00:22:13.510 --> 00:22:16.390
Farewell, eternal priestesses.

00:22:41.030 --> 00:22:47.740
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.740 --> 00:22:51.980
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:51.980 --> 00:22:59.050
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.050 --> 00:23:06.640
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.460 --> 00:23:19.540
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:24.710
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.710 --> 00:23:28.690
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.690 --> 00:23:32.720
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.720 --> 00:23:38.590
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.590 --> 00:23:44.140
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.140 --> 00:23:47.570
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.570 --> 00:23:53.240
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.240 --> 00:23:59.470
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:06.630
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:05.960 --> 00:24:07.300
This is…

00:24:07.300 --> 00:24:10.510
…the tale of the
sibyllae’s “tomorrow.”

00:24:12.680 --> 00:24:15.470
Next time, on the final
episode of Simoun…

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:19.970
<b>Their Portraits</b>

00:24:16.290 --> 00:24:18.180
Their Portraits.
